{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-08-22T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At Katmai National Park, crowd-pleasers don't need a stage. Brown bears wait by the river, and when the salmon jump, the show begins.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_EN-GB1247114173_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_EN-GB1247114173_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Meet Katmai's fishing giants","Title":"Brown bear fishing in river, Katmai National Park, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© Pal Hermansen/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/58.585845,-154.920897/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=58.585845,-154.920897;S9;Katmai National Park, Alaska, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Katmai+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260822_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear"},"Ssd":"20260823","Name":"KatmaiBear","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1247114173","FullDateString":"23 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"That quick glimpse of blue fluttering through a field has a story that begins much earlier, with a tiny caterpillar and an unexpected partnership. The common blue butterfly (Polyommatus icarus), named after Icarus, the figure from Greek mythology, is found across Europe, North Africa and parts of Asia. It begins life as an egg laid on host plants such as common bird's-foot trefoil. After hatching, the caterpillar feeds on the leaves before producing a sugary substance that attracts ants. In return for this sweet reward, the ants often protect the developing caterpillar from predators during one of the most vulnerable stages of its life. Depending on the climate, the species can produce two or three generations between spring and autumn.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CommonBlue_EN-GB1147628721_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CommonBlue_EN-GB1147628721_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Sky tinted wings","Title":"Common blue butterfly, Devon, England","Copyright":"© Ross Hoddinott/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Despite their delicate appearance, males of common blue butterflies actively chase away rival males—and sometimes even larger insects—from favourable patches of flowers.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260822_CommonBlue\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Common+blue+butterfly&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260821_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260822_CommonBlue"},"Ssd":"20260822","Name":"CommonBlue","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1147628721","FullDateString":"22 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some mountain roads become destinations in their own right, and Julier Pass is one of them. Rising to 2,284 metres, this Swiss mountain pass has connected Alpine valleys for nearly 2,000 years. Long before modern traffic, Roman travellers, merchants and messengers crossed its heights. Archaeological discoveries, including hundreds of Roman coins and the remains of two stone columns, suggest there was once a sanctuary or resting place for those making the climb. The summit also marks the major European watershed dividing the Rhine and Danube river basins.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.JulierPass_EN-GB1060938084_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.JulierPass_EN-GB1060938084_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The climb is calling","Title":"Winding road of Julier Pass, Switzerland","Copyright":"© Westend61/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/46.471172,9.725359/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=46.471172,9.725359;S9;Julier Pass, Switzerland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260821_JulierPass\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Julier+Pass+Switzerland&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260820_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260821_JulierPass"},"Ssd":"20260821","Name":"JulierPass","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1060938084","FullDateString":"21 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"An orca breaks the surface of Lynn Canal against the backdrop of the snow-capped Chilkat Mountains in Southeast Alaska, United States. Also known as the killer whale, the orca is the largest member of the dolphin family and one of the ocean's most recognisable predators. The cold, nutrient-rich waters of Alaska's Inside Passage provide abundant feeding grounds, sustaining salmon runs and a rich variety of marine life that supports these remarkable animals.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LynnCanalOrca_EN-GB6204959413_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LynnCanalOrca_EN-GB6204959413_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Voices of the pod","Title":"An orca surfaces in Lynn Canal near the Chilkat Mountains, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© John Hyde/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/58.69194,-135.097504/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=58.69194,-135.097504;S9;Lynn Canal, Alaska, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260820_LynnCanalOrca\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Orca+animal&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260819_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260820_LynnCanalOrca"},"Ssd":"20260820","Name":"LynnCanalOrca","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6204959413","FullDateString":"20 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The best route here isn't built with concrete. Instead, the tide reveals a rocky path leading from Whytecliff Park to Whyte Islet in West Vancouver, Canada. A few hours later, the sea quietly covers the crossing again, making timing part of the experience. This shoreline has drawn visitors for generations. The tide opens the path; wet rocks keep you humble. The reward is a sweeping view back towards the beach and the hillside homes of Gleneagles.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_EN-GB6122204864_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_EN-GB6122204864_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A path between the waves","Title":"Whytecliff Park in West Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada","Copyright":"© Aolin Chen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/49.375514,-123.288861/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=49.375514,-123.288861;S9;Whytecliff Park, West Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260819_WhyteCliffP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whytecliff+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260818_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260819_WhyteCliffP"},"Ssd":"20260819","Name":"WhyteCliffP","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"6122204864","FullDateString":"19 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From above, Palmanova looks less like a town and more like a carefully drawn star set into the plains of Friuli-Venezia Giulia, Italy. Founded by the Republic of Venice in 1593, this fortress city was designed for defence, order and spectacle. Its streets radiate from a central square, while its walls are shaped into a precise nine-pointed pattern. That geometry was no accident. Palmanova became one of the most influential models of early modern military architecture. It was protected by concentric fortifications built first under Venice and later strengthened and expanded during the Napoleonic period.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Palmanova_EN-GB5986280332_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Palmanova_EN-GB5986280332_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Geometry of a star city","Title":"Aerial view of Palmanova, a fortress city in Friuli, Italy","Copyright":"© Riccardo Saponi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/45.907204,13.311111/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=45.907204,13.311111;S9;Palmanova, Friuli-Venezia Giulia, Italy&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260818_Palmanova\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Palmanova+Italy&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260817_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260818_Palmanova"},"Ssd":"20260818","Name":"Palmanova","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5986280332","FullDateString":"18 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Location matters. Just ask the false clownfish seen in the image at Lighthouse Reef, near Cabilao Island, Philippines. In these tropical waters packed with hungry mouths and fierce competition, they've secured prime real estate: a sea anemone armed with thousands of microscopic stinging cells.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CabilaoClowns_EN-GB5900354557_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CabilaoClowns_EN-GB5900354557_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A prime 'reef' estate","Title":"Three false clownfish in a sea anemone, Cabilao Island, Bohol, Philippines","Copyright":"© Franco Banfi/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/9.881099,123.771501/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=9.881099,123.771501;S9;Cabilao Island, Bohol, Philippines&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260817_CabilaoClowns\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=False+clownfish&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260816_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260817_CabilaoClowns"},"Ssd":"20260817","Name":"CabilaoClowns","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"5900354557","FullDateString":"17 Aug 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today, International Whale Shark Day makes room for the world's largest fish. Despite their name, whale sharks are not whales but fish, reaching lengths of up to 18 metres and weighing around 18 tonnes. Found in warm tropical seas, they glide through the water with their mouths open, filtering plankton, fish eggs and other tiny prey. This species' distinctive white-spot patterns are unique to each individual, much like human fingerprints.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-GB1905405727_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-GB1905405727_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The fish that outgrew its name","Title":"Whale shark and golden trevally, Cenderawasih Bay, West Papua, Indonesia","Copyright":"© Pete Oxford/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Whale sharks may live for a century or more, giving the world's largest fish an unexpectedly long life span.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whale+shark&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260829_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark"},"Ssd":"20260830","Name":"YellowShark","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1905405727","FullDateString":"30 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some weekends ask you to slow down. This one turns the volume up. Streets become dance floors, steel pans replace traffic noise, and the scent of Caribbean food follows every step. At Notting Hill Carnival, London's roads don't just close to traffic, they open to celebration.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NottingHillCarnival2026_EN-GB1828107135_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NottingHillCarnival2026_EN-GB1828107135_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A city painted in rhythm","Title":"Notting Hill Carnival, London","Copyright":"© Sebastian Remme/Alamy Live News","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.507408,-0.127724/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.507408,-0.127724;S9;London&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260829_NottingHillCarnival2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Notting+Hill+Carnival&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260828_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260829_NottingHillCarnival2026"},"Ssd":"20260829","Name":"NottingHillCarnival2026","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1828107135","FullDateString":"29 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At sunset, Mont-Saint‑Michel rises from the waters of Normandy, France, like a fortress shaped by the sea. Perched on a rocky tidal island, the abbey and village stand at the centre of one of Europe's most dramatic coastal settings. Twice a day, the sea retreats to reveal vast stretches of sand before surging back to reclaim the landscape. At high tide, the mount becomes an island once again. For centuries, travellers timed their journeys to this rhythm, crossing the flats when conditions allowed and watching the sea return hours later.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_EN-GB1738815139_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_EN-GB1738815139_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where tides shape a legend","Title":"Mont-Saint-Michel during high tide, Manche, Normandy, France","Copyright":"© Clement LEONARD/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.637417,-1.5112/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.637417,-1.5112;S9;Mont-Saint-Michel, Normandy, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mont+Saint+Michel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260827_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset"},"Ssd":"20260828","Name":"MichelSunset","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1738815139","FullDateString":"28 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Imagine a world without the natural wonders that hold about 90% of Earth's surface freshwater. Lakes are among our planet's most valuable resources, providing clean water, supporting wildlife, regulating climate and sustaining communities worldwide. Recognising their importance, the United Nations designated 27 August as World Lake Day, first observed in 2025. Earth is home to more than 117 million lakes covering nearly 4% of its land surface. Together, they sustain countless ecosystems, while Lake Baikal in Russia alone holds about one-fifth of the world's surface liquid freshwater. Yet many lakes face growing pressure from pollution, overuse and climate change.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_EN-GB1628809720_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_EN-GB1628809720_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Water, wildlife and wonder","Title":"Lesser flamingo flock, Lake Magadi, Kenya","Copyright":"© Denis-Huot/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-1.902409,36.265224/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-1.902409,36.265224;S9;Lake Magadi, Kenya&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Lake+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260826_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi"},"Ssd":"20260827","Name":"LakeMagadi","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1628809720","FullDateString":"27 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As darker nights return to Iceland, visitors will soon look to the skies for a chance to see the aurora borealis. Better known as the northern lights, this luminous phenomenon occurs when charged particles from the sun collide with oxygen and nitrogen high in Earth's atmosphere, creating shimmering ribbons of green, pink, purple and sometimes red light. From September to April, Iceland's northern location and long winter nights make it one of the world's finest places to witness the display.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_EN-GB1541173608_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_EN-GB1541173608_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A sky alive with colour","Title":"Auroras over Kirkjufell, Iceland","Copyright":"© Cavan Images/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/64.939949,-23.307478/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=64.939949,-23.307478;S9;Kirkjufell, Iceland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Aurora+borealis&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260825_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland"},"Ssd":"20260826","Name":"AurorasIceland","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1541173608","FullDateString":"26 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Off the coast of Santa Catarina in southern Brazil, the image captures a familiar ritual: surfers waiting beyond the breaking waves, their boards rising and falling with the Atlantic. From above, almost nothing seems to happen. But that's when the real work begins.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatarina_EN-GB1458336075_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatarina_EN-GB1458336075_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Reading between the waves","Title":"Aerial view of surfers, Santa Catarina, Brazil","Copyright":"© Wonderful Nature/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-27.374188,-48.654926/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-GB&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-27.374188,-48.654926;S9;Santa Catarina, Brazil&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260825_SantaCatarina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brazil+Santa+Catarina&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260824_2300\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260825_SantaCatarina"},"Ssd":"20260825","Name":"SantaCatarina","Market":"EN-GB","Hash":"1458336075","FullDateString":"25 Aug 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Brooklyn Bridge doesn't just connect Manhattan and Brooklyn in the United States—it bridges history, engineering and a few surprising stories too. Opened in 1883 after 14 years of construction, it became the world's first steel-wire suspension bridge, forever changing the way New Yorkers crossed the East River.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BKBridge_EN-GB1324235273_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BKBridge_EN-GB1324235273_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Crossing into history","Title":"Brooklyn Bridge, New York City, United States","Copyright":"© shayes17/Getty Images","SocialGoo